# No Lazy Initialization

A config, asset, or service that the game **always needs** is resolved once at a deterministic startup point — never behind a null-check-per-access getter.

Lazy getters cost a branch plus (for Unity objects) an engine-call `==` on **every access**, often in per-frame paths. Worse, they hide initialization order, move load hitches from startup to a random mid-gameplay first use, and delay missing-asset failures until whichever code path happens to touch the getter first.

```csharp
// ❌ BAD — pays a Unity null-check per access; fails at first use, mid-game
public static HudConfig Hud
{
    get
    {
        if (_hud == null)
        {
            _hud = ResourceManager.Load<HudConfig>(HudConfig.Address);
        }
        return _hud;
    }
}

// ✅ GOOD — loaded once before the first scene Awake; accessor is branch-free;
// a missing asset throws at startup (fail fast), not mid-game
public static HudConfig Hud { get; private set; }

[RuntimeInitializeOnLoadMethod(RuntimeInitializeLoadType.BeforeSceneLoad)]
static void Initialize()
{
    Hud = ResourceManager.Load<HudConfig>(HudConfig.Address);
}
```

## Where to initialize

| State | Init point |
|---|---|
| Static config/service caches | `[RuntimeInitializeOnLoadMethod(BeforeSceneLoad)]` |
| Instance fields on a MonoBehaviour | `Awake` / `OnSingletonAwake` |
| Scene references | Serialized fields, validated in `Awake` |

Pair every eager static with the project's static-reset hub (see domain-reload rule) — `RuntimeInitializeOnLoadMethod` re-runs on each play entry, so re-initialization is automatic.

## Allowed exceptions (narrow)

- **Genuinely optional or rarely-hit heavy content** (streamed assets, on-demand levels) — use an explicit `Load`/`Try*` call at the decision point, not a silent null check inside a getter.
- **Editor-only tooling** where startup cost matters more than per-access cost.

If the object is used every session, "maybe we won't need it" is not an argument — load it up front and fail loudly if it's missing.

## Agent checklist

- [ ] No new `if (_x == null) _x = Load(...)` getters for always-needed state
- [ ] Statics resolved in a `BeforeSceneLoad` initializer; instance fields in `Awake`
- [ ] Missing required assets throw/log at startup, not on first use
- [ ] Eager statics wired into the static-reset hub
